      { id:"q129", num:129, type:"multi", question:"What two ICMPv6 message types must be permitted through IPv6 ACLs to allow resolution of Layer 3 to Layer 2 addresses? (Choose two.)", answers:["neighbor solicitations","echo requests","neighbor advertisements","echo replies","router solicitations","router advertisements"], correct:["neighbor solicitations","neighbor advertisements"] },
      { id:"q130", num:130, type:"single", question:"After a SLAAC address has been generated and applied, what must the client do before it can begin to use this IPv6 address?", answers:["It must send a DHCPv6 INFORMATION-REQUEST message to request the address of the DNS server.","It must send a DHCPv6 REQUEST message to the DHCPv6 server to request permission to use this address.","It must send an ICMPv6 Router Solicitation message to determine what default gateway it should use.","It must send an ICMPv6 Neighbor Solicitation message to ensure that the address is not already in use on the network."], correct:["It must send an ICMPv6 Neighbor Solicitation message to ensure that the address is not already in use on the network."] },
      { id:"q131", num:131, type:"single", question:"First ping to default gateway failed; second ping to a host outside the local network was successful. What is a possible cause?", answers:["The default gateway is not operational.","The default gateway device is configured with the wrong IP address.","Security rules are applied to the default gateway device, preventing it from processing ping requests.","The TCP/IP stack on the default gateway is not working properly."], correct:["Security rules are applied to the default gateway device, preventing it from processing ping requests."] },
      { id:"q132", num:132, type:"single", question:"An organization is assigned IPv6 address block 2001:db8:0:ca00::/56. How many subnets can be created without using bits in the interface ID space?", answers:["256","512","1024","4096"], correct:["256"] },
      { id:"q133", num:133, type:"single", question:"What subnet mask is needed if an IPv4 network has 40 devices and address space is not to be wasted?", answers:["255.255.255.0","255.255.255.240","255.255.255.128","255.255.255.192","255.255.255.224"], correct:["255.255.255.192"] },
      { id:"q134", num:134, type:"single", image:"q134.png", question:"Refer to the exhibit. If host A sends an IP packet to host B, what will the destination address be in the frame when it leaves host A?", answers:["DD:DD:DD:DD:DD:DD","172.168.10.99","CC:CC:CC:CC:CC:CC","172.168.10.65","BB:BB:BB:BB:BB:BB","AA:AA:AA:AA:AA:AA"], correct:["CC:CC:CC:CC:CC:CC"] },
      { id:"q135", num:135, type:"single", question:"What is a benefit of using cloud computing in networking?", answers:["Technology is integrated into every-day appliances allowing them to interconnect with other devices.","Network capabilities are extended without requiring investment in new infrastructure, personnel, or software.","End users have the freedom to use personal tools to access information and communicate across a business network.","Home networking uses existing electrical wiring to connect devices to the network wherever there is an electrical outlet."], correct:["Network capabilities are extended without requiring investment in new infrastructure, personnel, or software."] },
      { id:"q136", num:136, type:"multi", question:"Which two statements are correct about MAC and IP addresses during data transmission if NAT is not involved? (Choose two.)", answers:["Destination IP addresses in a packet header remain constant along the entire path to a target host.","Destination MAC addresses will never change in a frame that goes across seven routers.","Every time a frame is encapsulated with a new destination MAC address, a new destination IP address is needed.","Destination and source MAC addresses have local significance and change every time a frame goes from one LAN to another.","A packet that has crossed four routers has changed the destination IP address four times."], correct:["Destination IP addresses in a packet header remain constant along the entire path to a target host.","Destination and source MAC addresses have local significance and change every time a frame goes from one LAN to another."] },
      { id:"q137", num:137, type:"single", question:"What is one main characteristic of the data link layer?", answers:["It generates the electrical or optical signals that represent the 1 and 0 on the media.","It converts a stream of data bits into a predefined code.","It shields the upper layer protocol from being aware of the physical medium to be used in the communication.","It accepts Layer 3 packets and decides the path by which to forward the packet to a remote network."], correct:["It shields the upper layer protocol from being aware of the physical medium to be used in the communication."] },
      { id:"q138", num:138, type:"multi", question:"What are three characteristics of the CSMA/CD process? (Choose three.)", answers:["The device with the electronic token is the only one that can transmit after a collision.","A device listens and waits until the media is not busy before transmitting.","After detecting a collision, hosts can attempt to resume transmission after a random time delay has expired.","All of the devices on a segment see data that passes on the network medium.","A jam signal indicates that the collision has cleared and the media is not busy.","Devices can be configured with a higher transmission priority."], correct:["A device listens and waits until the media is not busy before transmitting.","After detecting a collision, hosts can attempt to resume transmission after a random time delay has expired.","All of the devices on a segment see data that passes on the network medium."] },
      { id:"q139", num:139, type:"single", question:"Which information does the show startup-config command display?", answers:["the IOS image copied into RAM","the bootstrap program in the ROM","the contents of the current running configuration file in the RAM","the contents of the saved configuration file in the NVRAM"], correct:["the contents of the saved configuration file in the NVRAM"] },
      { id:"q140", num:140, type:"multi", question:"Which two commands can be used on a Windows host to display the routing table? (Choose two.)", answers:["netstat -s","route print","show ip route","netstat -r","tracert"], correct:["route print","netstat -r"] },
      { id:"q141", num:141, type:"multi", question:"What are two functions provided by the network layer? (Choose two.)", answers:["directing data packets to destination hosts on other networks","placing data on the network medium","carrying data between processes that are running on source and destination hosts","providing dedicated end-to-end connections","providing end devices with a unique network identifier"], correct:["directing data packets to destination hosts on other networks","providing end devices with a unique network identifier"] },
      { id:"q142", num:142, type:"multi", question:"Which two statements describe features of an IPv4 routing table on a router? (Choose two.)", answers:["Directly connected interfaces will have two route source codes in the routing table: C and S.","If there are two or more possible routes to the same destination, the route associated with the higher metric value is included in the routing table.","The netstat -r command can be used to display the routing table of a router.","The routing table lists the MAC addresses of each active interface.","It stores information about routes derived from the active router interfaces.","If a default static route is configured in the router, an entry will be included in the routing table with source code S."], correct:["It stores information about routes derived from the active router interfaces.","If a default static route is configured in the router, an entry will be included in the routing table with source code S."] },
      { id:"q143", num:143, type:"single", question:"What characteristic describes a VPN?", answers:["software on a router that filters traffic based on IP addresses or applications","software that identifies fast-spreading threats","a tunneling protocol that provides remote users with secure access into the network of an organization","a network device that filters access and traffic coming into a network"], correct:["a tunneling protocol that provides remote users with secure access into the network of an organization"] },
      { id:"q144", num:144, type:"single", question:"Why would a Layer 2 switch need an IP address?", answers:["to enable the switch to send broadcast frames to attached PCs","to enable the switch to function as a default gateway","to enable the switch to be managed remotely","to enable the switch to receive frames from attached PCs"], correct:["to enable the switch to be managed remotely"] },
      { id:"q145", num:145, type:"drag", question:"Match each description to its corresponding term. (Not all options are used.)", image:"match-q145.png", pairs:[["the process of placing one message format inside another message format","message encapsulation"],["the process of breaking up a long message into individual pieces before being sent over the network","message sizing"],["the process of converting information from one format into another acceptable for transmission","message encoding"]], correct:{"the process of placing one message format inside another message format":"message encapsulation","the process of breaking up a long message into individual pieces before being sent over the network":"message sizing","the process of converting information from one format into another acceptable for transmission":"message encoding"} },
      { id:"q146", num:146, type:"single", question:"A user sends an HTTP request to a web server on a remote network. What information is added to the address field of a frame to indicate the destination?", answers:["the network domain of the destination host","the IP address of the default gateway","the MAC address of the destination host","the MAC address of the default gateway"], correct:["the MAC address of the default gateway"] },
      { id:"q147", num:147, type:"single", question:"What is an advantage to using a protocol defined by an open standard?", answers:["A company can monopolize the market.","The protocol can only be run on equipment from a specific vendor.","An open standard protocol is not controlled or regulated by standards organizations.","It encourages competition and promotes choices."], correct:["It encourages competition and promotes choices."] },
      { id:"q148", num:148, type:"multi", question:"Data is being sent from a source PC to a destination server. Which three statements correctly describe the function of TCP or UDP? (Choose three.)", answers:["The source port field identifies the running application or service that will handle data returning to the PC.","The TCP process running on the PC randomly selects the destination port when establishing a session with the server.","UDP segments are encapsulated within IP packets for transport across the network.","The UDP destination port number identifies the application or service on the server which will handle the data.","TCP is the preferred protocol when a function requires lower network overhead.","The TCP source port number identifies the sending host on the network."], correct:["The source port field identifies the running application or service that will handle data returning to the PC.","UDP segments are encapsulated within IP packets for transport across the network.","The UDP destination port number identifies the application or service on the server which will handle the data."] },
      { id:"q149", num:149, type:"drag", question:"Match each description with the corresponding TCP mechanism. (Not all options are used.)", image:"match-q149.png", pairs:[["number of bytes a destination device can accept and process at one time","window size"],["used to identify missing segments of data","sequence numbers"],["method of managing segments of data loss","retransmission"],["received by a sender before transmitting more segments in a session","acknowledgment"]], correct:{"number of bytes a destination device can accept and process at one time":"window size","used to identify missing segments of data":"sequence numbers","method of managing segments of data loss":"retransmission","received by a sender before transmitting more segments in a session":"acknowledgment"} },
      { id:"q150", num:150, type:"single", image:"q150.png", question:"Refer to the exhibit. A company uses address block 128.107.0.0/16. What subnet mask would provide the maximum number of equal size subnets while providing enough host addresses for the largest subnet shown?", answers:["255.255.255.192","255.255.255.0","255.255.255.128","255.255.255.240","255.255.255.224"], correct:["255.255.255.128"] },
      { id:"q151", num:151, type:"single", question:"Largest subnetwork has 10 addresses. What single subnet mask is appropriate for three subnetworks?", answers:["255.255.255.0","255.255.255.240","255.255.255.248","255.255.255.252"], correct:["255.255.255.240"] },
      { id:"q152", num:152, type:"drag", question:"Match each item to the type of topology diagram on which it is typically identified. (Not all options are used.)", image:"match-q152.png", pairs:[["location of a desktop PC in a classroom","physical topology diagram"],["path of cables that connect rooms to wiring closets","physical topology diagram"],["IP address of a server","logical topology diagram"]], correct:{"location of a desktop PC in a classroom":"physical topology diagram","path of cables that connect rooms to wiring closets":"physical topology diagram","IP address of a server":"logical topology diagram"} },
      { id:"q153", num:153, type:"multi", question:"What two pieces of information are displayed in the output of the show ip interface brief command? (Choose two.)", answers:["IP addresses","interface descriptions","MAC addresses","next-hop addresses","Layer 1 statuses","speed and duplex settings"], correct:["IP addresses","Layer 1 statuses"] },
      { id:"q154", num:154, type:"single", question:"A web page is taking longer than normal to load but eventually loads. Which tool should the technician use to locate where the issue is in the network?", answers:["ping","nslookup","tracert","ipconfig /displaydns"], correct:["tracert"] },
      { id:"q155", num:155, type:"single", question:"Which value in an IPv4 header field is decremented by each router that receives a packet?", answers:["Header Length","Differentiated Services","Time-to-Live","Fragment Offset"], correct:["Time-to-Live"] },
      { id:"q156", num:156, type:"multi", question:"Which two issues should be considered before implementing fiber optic media? (Choose two.)", answers:["Fiber optic cabling requires different termination and splicing expertise from what copper cabling requires.","Fiber optic cabling requires specific grounding to be immune to EMI.","Fiber optic cabling is susceptible to loss of signal due to RFI.","Fiber optic cable is able to withstand rough handling.","Fiber optic provides higher data capacity but is more expensive than copper cabling."], correct:["Fiber optic cabling requires different termination and splicing expertise from what copper cabling requires.","Fiber optic provides higher data capacity but is more expensive than copper cabling."] },
      { id:"q157", num:157, type:"drag", question:"Match each description with an appropriate IP address. (Not all options are used.)", image:"match-q157.png", pairs:[["an experimental address","240.2.6.255"],["a link-local address","169.254.1.5"],["a public address","198.133.219.2"],["a loopback address","127.0.0.1"]], correct:{"an experimental address":"240.2.6.255","a link-local address":"169.254.1.5","a public address":"198.133.219.2","a loopback address":"127.0.0.1"} },
      { id:"q158", num:158, type:"single", question:"At what point would a router in the path stop forwarding the packet during a tracert?", answers:["when the router receives an ICMP Time Exceeded message","when the RTT value reaches zero","when the host responds with an ICMP Echo Reply message","when the value in the TTL field reaches zero","when the values of both the Echo Request and Echo Reply messages reach zero"], correct:["when the value in the TTL field reaches zero"] },
      { id:"q159", num:159, type:"single", question:"An employee downloaded a third-party scanning program for the printer, causing slow network performance. What type of malware might have been introduced?", answers:["virus","worm","phishing","spam"], correct:["worm"] }
